return {
    ["\n3月4日：翻完了前三十六任的全部维护日志，没有发现任何异常。但那一夜它确实出了问题。答案不在日志里。那答案在哪里？\n\n3月11日：典籍里关于知识皇冠的记载只有只言片语——为什么这么少？是被删掉了吗？谁删的？必须找到更原始的文本。\n\n3月19日：十一本。还差一本。\n\n3月26日：不能停。停下来就会，就会？不能停。\n\n4月2日：它就在某个地方。找到它找到它找到它——\n\n4月3日：一定要找到它。\n\n（后面还有很多页，但字迹越来越潦草，到最后已经很难辨认。）"] = "\nMarch 4: Finished reading all the maintenance logs of the first 36 predecessors, found no abnormalities. But it really did have a problem that night. The answer is not in the logs. Where is the answer?\n\nMarch 11: The records in the classics about the Crown of Knowledge are only fragments—why so few? Was it deleted? Who deleted it? Must find more primitive texts.\n\nMarch 19: Eleven books. Still missing one.\n\nMarch 26: Cannot stop. If I stop, I will, I will? Cannot stop.\n\nApril 2: It is somewhere. Find it find it find it—\n\nApril 3: Must find it.\n\n(There are many pages behind, but the handwriting is getting more and more illegible, and it is hard to recognize by the end.)",
    ["\n　　嘿，我亲爱的玩家！\n　　既然你要和“国王”玩选择游戏，不了解规则可不行。所以我亲自为你编写了这份终极傻瓜……哦不，是《终极扑克速成指南》！\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>五条</>：五张完全一样的扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>顺子</>：数字连续的五张扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>同花</>：花色相同的五张扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>同花顺</>：花色相同，且数字连续的五张扑克。\n\n　　祝你好运……或者，祝你能看穿“好运”背后的把戏！"] = "\n　　Hey, my dear player!\n　　Since you are going to play a choice game with the \"King\", you can't do it without knowing the rules. So I personally wrote this ultimate dummy... oh no, it's the \"Ultimate Poker Quick Guide\" for you!\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Five of a Kind</>: Five identical poker cards.\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Straight</>: Five poker cards with consecutive numbers.\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Flush</>: Five poker cards of the same suit.\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Straight Flush</>: Five poker cards of the same suit and consecutive numbers.\n\n　　Good luck... or, I hope you can see through the tricks behind \"good luck\"!",
    ["%s:\n      我听闻你与异化猎犬遭遇了一场苦战。不必过分担忧。在过去的岁月循环中，我已经明白失败与胜利——乃至生存与死亡——都不过是一时的、相对的：它只是你旅途中的一个普通坐标，用来验证你的成长。谨记面对异化猎犬的诀窍：<HyperLink stylename=\"M_Link\" u=\"jump=1302115\">异化猎犬的记载</>\n      对于一位总在路上的旅人来说，我知道让人停下脚步的常常并非挫折本身，而是失去了再次上路的勇气。所幸你并不胆怯于面对更多新冒险，我想下次，我听到的就会是更好的消息。对你这样年轻的非凡者而言，你已经做得很好。\n      如果你需要的话，漫长的时光为我积淀下一些经验，也许对你有用。<HyperLink stylename=\"M_Link\" u=\"jump=1250207\">点此查看</>"] = "%s:\n      I heard that you encountered a bitter battle with the Alienated Hound. Do not worry too much. In the cycles of time past, I have come to understand that failure and victory—and even life and death—are merely temporary and relative: they are just ordinary coordinates on your journey, used to verify your growth. Keep in mind the tips for facing the Alienated Hound: <HyperLink stylename=\"M_Link\" u=\"jump=1302115\">Records of the Alienated Hound</>\n      For a traveler who is always on the road, I know that what makes people stop is often not the setback itself, but the loss of courage to set off again. Fortunately, you are not timid about facing new adventures, and I think next time, the news I hear will be better. For a young Beyonder like you, you have already done very well. \n      If you need it, the long passage of time has accumulated some experience for me that might be useful to you. <HyperLink stylename=\"M_Link\" u=\"jump=1250207\">Click here to view</>",
